 EVALUATION PROCEDURE                                             9040 1451  149
                                                                  9040 1451  150
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9040 1451  151
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9040 1451  152
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9040 1451  153
                                                                  9040 1451  154
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              9040 1451  155
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b33 by                    9040 1451  156
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               9040 1451  157
 into a single system a number of important modules               9040 1451  158
 and features, relevant for this evaluation:                      9040 1451  159
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9040 1451  160
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         9040 1451  161
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9040 1451  162
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              9040 1451  163
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9040 1451  164
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9040 1451  165
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9040 1451  166
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9040 1451  167
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9040 1451  168
   discrete transitions                                           9040 1451  169
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              9040 1451  170
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9040 1451  171
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9040 1451  172
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              9040 1451  173
   library [Ri03]                                                 9040 1451  174
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9040 1451  175
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           9040 1451  176
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    9040 1451  177
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9040 1451  178
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9040 1451  179
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      9040 1451  180
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        9040 1451  181
 - Support for NJOY                                               9040 1451  182
                                                                  9040 1451  183
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                9040 1451  184
                                                                  9040 1451  185
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 9040 1451  186
 current evaluation:                                              9040 1451  187
                                                                  9040 1451  188
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-2 level                 9040 1451  189
 file, based on the 1998 version of ENSDF.                        9040 1451  190
 Prompt fission neutron spectra and niu-bar                       9040 1451  191
 calculation include contributions from thorium                   9040 1451  192
 and actinium chain (see description of the method                9040 1451  193
 used in Maslov V.M. et al, Eur.Phys.J.A18(2003)93).              9040 1451  194
 Niu-bar calculation was renormalized to evaluation               9040 1451  195
 based on experimental data (see niu-bar section)                 9040 1451  196
 Prefission neutrons assumed anisotropic following                9040 1451  197
 (n,xn) angular distribution.                                     9040 1451  198
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9040 1451  199
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      9040 1451  200
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            9040 1451  201
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           9040 1451  202
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS energy dependent              9040 1451  203
 (it was increased around 14 +/- 3 MeV to reproduce               9040 1451  204
 energy dependence of n,2n cross section)                         9040 1451  205
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 1.95 MeV        9040 1451  206
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  3             9040 1451  207
 Shell corrections according to Myers-Swiatecki                   9040 1451  208
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from 233Th multiplied by   3.330    9040 1451  209
 Emission width of ejectile 2 from 233Th multiplied by   1.500    9040 1451  210
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     9040 1451  211
 Direct contributions to continuum were smoothed using            9040 1451  212
 gaussian function                                                9040 1451  213
 For all nuclei: advanced treatment of fission                    9040 1451  214
 E1 strength function set to MLO1                                 9040 1451  215
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           9040 1451  216
